WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.802
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
My name is Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:05.738
Hi.
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:09.109
Well, guys,
after months of speculation,

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:11.111
Joe Biden finally
made the announcement

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.611
we've all been waiting for.

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:14.414
-We're coming on the air
with breaking news.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.983
Democratic
presidential candidate Joe Biden

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:19.819
has made his choice.
NBC News has confirmed

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:23.356
that Biden has picked
California Senator Kamala Harris

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.892
to be his running mate,
the first woman of color

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:29.496
in history to be chosen
for such a position.

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:31.564
-That's right,
Joe Biden has selected

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:34.100
Senator Kamala Harris
as his running mate.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.635
Kamala is the daughter
of two immigrants,

00:00:36.635 --> 00:00:39.572
she went to Howard University,
she's a Democratic senator

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.873
from California.

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:42.975
It's an inspiring story,
unless you're Trump.

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:44.644
Then it's a Stephen King novel.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.580
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.115
Yeah, in a statement,
Kamala said,

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.617
"I'm very much looking forward
to serving as President --

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:55.688
Vice -- Vice President!
I mean, Vice President."

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:58.724
Biden announced his selection
in a tweet and called Kamala

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:01.828
"a fearless fighter
for the little guy."

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:04.097
And Dr. Fauci was like,
"Thank you."

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:07.166
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:09.002
She's only had the job
for a few hours,

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:12.104
but Kamala's already gearing up
for her debate with Mike Pence.

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:13.405
That's why she spent
the entire day

00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:15.241
arguing with a mannequin
at Kohl's.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.910
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.179
Yeah, Kamala Harris
has been chosen by Joe Biden

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:22.481
as his running mate
and potential vice president.

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:24.617
Biden was quick to hold
a virtual press conference

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.019
to discuss his decision,

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.620
and people were very excited
to talk about it.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.721
Take a look.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.823
-Hey, folks,
thanks four for joining me

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.092
on your Zoom boxes.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:35.227
I'm sure you're all
buzzing like a honey pot

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:37.096
to talk about Kamala.

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:39.199
You know, I'm thrilled to
announce her as my running mate

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:41.300
and can't wait
for all the excitement

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.970
and experience
she brings to the team.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.839
But before I --
-Mr. Vice President,

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:47.674
what are Kamala's
plans for the country

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.241
once she gets
into the White House?

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:53.046
-Well, uh...
Kamala and I will work together,

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.913
hand in hand, in the White House

00:01:54.913 --> 00:01:57.383
to restore
the soul of this nation.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.718
-Mr. Vice President,
how does it feel

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.753
to be reaching this exciting
moment in your campaign?

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.089
Kamala Harris, wow.
-Well, you know, I thought

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.391
we were running a pretty
exciting campaign before this,

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.226
but --
-That's all.

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:09.395
-Okay.
-Excuse me, Mr. Biden?

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.030
I have a foreign-policy
question.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.166
-Yeah, now we're talkin'.
-Has Kamala asked about me?

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:16.903
-Asked about you?
No.

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.738
How is that
a foreign-policy question?

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.740
-Oh, I was just hoping
to take a trip with her.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.809
-All right, come on.
-Vice President Biden,

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.544
when you are the president...
-Thank you.

00:02:25.544 --> 00:02:30.182
-...I think Kamala Harris
is amazing and inspiring.

00:02:30.182 --> 00:02:31.450
-Is that a question?

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.654
-I think Kamala Harris
is amazing and inspiring?

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:37.656
-Okay.
-Is Kamala nice in person?

00:02:37.656 --> 00:02:40.659
-Geez.
Yes, she's very, very nice.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:42.361
-Knew it.
You can just tell.

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:43.496
Very kind eyes.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:47.066
-I have a question, mister --
mister...

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:48.467
Oh, my God.
What was your name again?

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.536
-Joe Biden.
-Of course -- Jim.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:53.439
My question is, is Kamala here?

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:56.009
-No, she's not.
-Aww!

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:59.178
-But I can send a link to her
virtual speech in the chat.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:00.779
-Yay!

00:03:00.779 --> 00:03:02.348
-All right.
Does anyone have a question

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.651
that is not about Kamala Harris?

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.719
-I do.
-Great. Shoot.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.622
-How is Barack Obama doing?
-Seriously?

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.858
-And follow-up question --
Do you think you would ever

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.459
want to be
the Vice President again?

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:16.962
Maybe, like, next?
-Okay, th-th-that's enough.

00:03:16.962 --> 00:03:19.465
I'm excited to have Kamala
running beside me

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.801
in this campaign,
and we will work together,

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.236
with me as the president

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:26.138
and Kamala Harris
as the vice president.

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:29.242
And that's how
it's going to go, okay?

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:30.243
Okay.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.945
-Madam President!
Madam President!

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:34.013
-I -- I think you're confused,
Jack.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:36.849
-No, I'm just practicing.
-But -- It's --

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:40.386
This is -- I know people
are excited about Kamala.

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.722
-Yay!

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.791
-Biden.

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:47.627
Kamala.
-Yay!

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:50.296
-All right, heck, I'm almost
taking this personal here.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.297
Listen, at the end of the day,

00:03:52.297 --> 00:03:54.967
I suppose old Joe
should take it as a compliment.

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:56.335
I believe in this woman,

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:58.871
even if she handed me my rear
at the debates.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:01.807
And together,
we can accomplish anything.

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:03.609
Thank you all for coming.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.077
I do have to go.

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:08.313
I am late
for another engagement.

00:04:08.313 --> 00:04:11.951
Thank you all for coming.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.285
[ Clicking ]

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:17.123
How do you get off this thing?
[ Clicking continues ]

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:20.426
Ah, hell.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.827
-Well, that was interesting.

00:04:21.827 --> 00:04:23.529
Well, guys,
here's some big news.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.765
It was announced today that
there's a new vaccine

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:28.568
to treat the coronavirus.
Sort of.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:30.937
-Breaking news this morning --
Vladimir Putin claiming

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.271
Russia has developed
and approved

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:34.273
the world's first
coronavirus vaccine,

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:37.510
a claim that is being met
with heavy skepticism,

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.712
despite Putin announcing
his own daughter

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.714
is among the first
to receive a dose.

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:43.449
-That's right.
Russia now claims

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:46.052
to have a coronavirus vaccine,
which is great.

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:47.854
'Cause if there's one thing
I know about Russia,

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.655
they never lie about drug tests.

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.190
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.226
Oh, no.

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.394
Vladimir Putin
defended the new vaccine.

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:56.462
He was like, "Don't worry.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.364
Just like upcoming
U.S. election,

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:03.136
results are totally legitimate.
[ Laughs ]

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.670
That's right,
the new COVID vaccine

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:08.140
has been approved by four
out of five Russian scientists.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.474
And in a related story,

00:05:09.474 --> 00:05:11.778
one out of five Russian
scientists are now missing.

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:17.416
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:19.252
-"What did you say?"

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:20.453
That's right --
over the course

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:22.655
of just under two months,
the vaccine was tested

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:26.025
on a couple dozen people,
some even willingly.

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:27.460
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.761
Just to prove it safe, Putin
said that one of his daughters

00:05:29.761 --> 00:05:31.730
actually got the vaccine.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:32.999
I don't know
much about his family,

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:35.768
but I know that that kid
is definitely his "Don Jr."

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.603
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:39.104
Maybe the vaccine will work.

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:40.205
So far,
the only side effects are

00:05:40.205 --> 00:05:42.641
depression, hunger, and chills.

00:05:42.641 --> 00:05:44.843
Although, in Putin's defense,
that's how everyone walked in

00:05:44.843 --> 00:05:46.345
before the vaccine, so...

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:47.546
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.546 --> 00:05:49.181
In his announcement,
Putin said, quote,

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:51.651
"It works effectively enough."

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:53.719
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.719 --> 00:05:56.655
That's like your doctor saying,
"I got most of the ringworm.

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:59.592
Yeah, well --
we'll be fine."

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:00.893
When asked about the vaccine,

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.995
the U.S. Secretary
of Health and Human Services

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:05.631
said, "The point is
not to be first."

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.032
And Trump was like,
"Yeah, yeah, great.

00:06:07.032 --> 00:06:10.436
A vaccine on my desk by lunch
or you're fired."

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.371
Speaking of the President,
last night, at the White House,

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:15.374
he tried to talk about
the 1918 pandemic,

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:17.276
and he was
a little off on his history.

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:18.644
Watch this.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:24.016
-The closest thing is, in 1917,
they say -- right? --

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:27.954
the great -- the great pandemic
certainly was a terrible thing.

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:29.956
Probably ended
the second World War.

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:31.524
All the soldiers were sick.

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:34.192
[ Laughter ]
-Aw, come on.

00:06:34.192 --> 00:06:36.628
-Not too bad.
He was only off by two decades.

00:06:36.628 --> 00:06:40.466
What's the big deal?
What, what, what?

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:42.201
"Congratulations.
It's a baby boy.

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:44.570
And he can vote."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.138
Trump's basically like
the baseball coach

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:48.007
who subs in when
the history teacher gets sick.

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:49.075
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:51.610
"All right,
World War II is, uh..."

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.113
Let's just put on a movie.
You guys like "Sandlot"?

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:56.248
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.248 --> 00:06:59.118
But Trump was like, "Those who
cannot remember the past

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:00.753
are condemned to retweet it."

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:02.955
At this point,
Trump's teleprompter

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:05.357
is just a shrug emoji.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:07.593
Then Trump said,
"And I believe the war ended

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:11.230
when President Truman uttered
his famous words,

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:15.034
'It is what it is.'"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:17.103
-Meanwhile,
Trump is thinking about a move

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:19.338
that would affect Americans
who traveled abroad.

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:20.672
Check this out.

00:07:20.672 --> 00:07:23.242
-The Trump administration
is now reportedly considering

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:25.778
a new rule that could block
American citizens

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:28.213
and permanent residents
from returning to the country

00:07:28.213 --> 00:07:31.751
if they are suspected
of having coronavirus.

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:34.854
-That's like if Pinterest said,
"Sorry. No more wedding stuff."

00:07:34.854 --> 00:07:36.755
[ Laughter ]

00:07:36.755 --> 00:07:38.090
Seriously.
That's like Walmart saying,

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.459
Nobody's allowed inside
with a barbed-wire tattoo."

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:42.828
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:44.863
That's like a Motel 6 saying,
"Look, we don't want

00:07:44.863 --> 00:07:46.565
anyone in here with bedbugs,
okay?"

00:07:46.565 --> 00:07:48.300
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.369
Yeah, but schools
and college football are fine.

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:53.139
It's Bob and Doreen coming home
from Toronto that's the problem.

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:54.473
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:56.375
And this is interesting.
It's only August, but check out

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:58.410
what's already
showing up in stores.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.781
-We're still in summer,
but Halloween candy displays

00:08:01.781 --> 00:08:05.217
have arrived even earlier
this year.

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:07.119
-Why do we even need
Halloween this year?

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:09.588
Every day, we're walking around
in a mask, completely terrified.

00:08:09.588 --> 00:08:11.924
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:13.459
Yeah, the good news is,
now you can walk in

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:15.093
to any pharmacy and get
Halloween candy.

00:08:15.093 --> 00:08:17.330
The bad news is,
still no Clorox wipes.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.764
[ Laughter ]

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:21.434
Meanwhile, CVS employees are
carrying Christmas trees like,

00:08:21.434 --> 00:08:22.935
"You guys still talking about
Halloween?"

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:25.370
[ Laughter ]

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:28.006
Listen to this -- a new study
shows that using mouthwash

00:08:28.006 --> 00:08:31.410
could reduce the risk
of contracting coronavirus.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:34.079
Study might be good news,
although now it feels like

00:08:34.079 --> 00:08:35.414
we're one press conference away

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:37.583
from Trump telling us
to inject Scope.

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.485
[ Laughter ]

00:08:39.485 --> 00:08:40.953
And finally,
this is pretty crazy.

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:44.823
A professional stuntman decided
to propose to his girlfriend

00:08:44.823 --> 00:08:47.426
after lighting himself on fire.

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:48.994
Take a look at this thing.

00:08:48.994 --> 00:08:50.963
Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.963 --> 00:08:52.464
And just to mess with him,
she was like,

00:08:52.464 --> 00:08:54.967
"Mm, let me think about it
for a sec."

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:56.769
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.769 --> 00:08:58.203
I'm kidding.
She said yes,

00:08:58.203 --> 00:09:01.107
and then things took a turn when
he jumped up and hugged her.

00:09:01.107 --> 00:09:03.409
[ Laughter ]

00:09:03.409 --> 00:09:05.844
No, no, it was cute right up
until she ran off

00:09:05.844 --> 00:09:08.180
with the fireman
who saved that guy's life.

